From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thibaut Lapierre <root@epheo.eu>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:45:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] multus: namespace isolation

Multus runs with namespace isolation, as OpenShift's network operator
renders it: a pod attaches only to NetworkAttachmentDefinitions in its own
namespace or in network.multus.globalNamespaces, which defaults to
OpenShift's list (default, openshift-multus,
openshift-sriov-network-operator, openshift-cnv). Upstream lets any pod
attach to any namespace's NAD by name, br-ex localnet networks included.

A non-empty globalNamespaces replaces the list. Multus reads an empty one
as "default", so a site that shares no namespace names an admin-only one.
Multus refuses a violating reference at CNI ADD: the pod is admitted, then
fails to start.

Upstream: no namespace isolation as of 5.0.
Covered by: config unit tests; vm-test (a pod naming another namespace's
NAD fails to start, its own namespace's and default's attach).
